<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-frīgesco</span></b> , frixi, 3,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>v. inch. n.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to grow very
			cold</i>, <i>to catch cold</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne canes perfrigescant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 9, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 31, 6, 33, § 66</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ei, qui perfrixit, opus est in laconico sedere,
					donec insudet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 1,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si perfrixit, cantat bene,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					7, 194</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (post-class.), M. Aur. ap. <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad M. Caes. 4, 5</span></i>.</div>
